directly to municipal issuers). Without admitting or denying any wrongdoing,
Morgan Stanley consented to the entry of an order directing that it cease and
desist from violating Sections 17(a)(2) and 17(a)(3) of the Securities Act of
1933 and requiring it to pay $2.45 million to the United States Treasury. No
payment to municipal issuers was required.



